## OPENDOCUMENT
opendocument [ASK | FILE "file"] [FILTER filtername] [STATUS | NOSTATUS]

Opens a document.
- ASK -- Opens file selection dialog
- FILE -- File name and path
- FILTER -- Filter: IFFDOC, PAGESTREAM2, PROPAGE, WORDWORTHDOC
- STATUS/NOSTATUS -- Progress indicator (default: NOSTATUS)

Example: opendocument FILE "Work:Documents/Newsletter.doc"

## OPEN
open [file] [FILTER ""] [optional module parameters]

Opens a document and creates a window.
- file -- File path (omit for file selection dialog, since v5.0.3.4)
- FILTER -- Filter specification

Example: open "PageStream:documents/Project.doc"

## CLOSEDOCUMENT
closedocument [mode] [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Closes all views of a document and the document itself.
- mode -- FORCE (without save prompt), ALERT (dialog if changes exist), QUIET (default: silent, error on unsaved changes)
- DOCUMENT -- Document name (default: current)
- WINDOW -- Window name (default: current)

Example: closedocument force document "project.doc"

## CLOSEWINDOW
closewindow [WINDOW name]

Closes a single view. The document remains open.

Example: closewindow window "Untitled~View.1"

## SAVEDOCUMENT
savedocument [ASK | FILE "file" | DEFAULT] [FILTER filtername]
            [STATUS | NOSTATUS] [QUIET | FORCE | ALERT]
            [TEMPLATE] [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec]

Saves an open document.
- ASK -- File selection dialog
- FILE -- File name and path
- DEFAULT -- Default save location
- FILTER -- Filter (default: IFFDOC)
- STATUS/NOSTATUS -- Progress indicator
- QUIET/FORCE/ALERT -- Overwrite behavior
- TEMPLATE -- Save as template

Example: savedocument file "Work:Documents/Project.doc" force

## REVERTDOCUMENT
revertdocument [STATUS | NOSTATUS] [FORCE | ALERT]
              [FILTER filtername]
              [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec]

Reloads the last saved version of a document.
- STATUS/NOSTATUS -- Progress indicator (default: NOSTATUS)
- FORCE/ALERT -- Confirmation mode (default: ALERT)
- FILTER -- Filter: IFFDOC, PAGESTREAM2, PROPAGE, WORDWORTHDOC

Example: revertdocument status quiet

## NEWDOCUMENT
newdocument [name]

Creates a new document. Returns the document name in RESULT. Does not create a default master page and does not open a window.

Example: newdocument "My Project"

## COLLECTOUTPUT
collectoutput [ASK | FILE "file"] [STATUS | NOSTATUS]
             [QUIET | FORCE | ALERT]
             [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec]

Collects all files for output (since PageStream 4.0).

## CHECKEXTERNALLINKS
checkexternallinks

Checks external links in the document.

## PLACEGRAPHIC
placegraphic [FILE "file"] [FILTER filtername]
            [STATUS | NOSTATUS]
            [ASIS | AT x y | USER]
            [PAGE pagespec | MPG masterpagespec | DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec]

Places a graphic file in a document.
- FILE -- File name and path (omit for file selection dialog)
- FILTER -- PICT, TIFF, IFFILBM, GIF, BMP, IFFDR2D, IFFILUS, JPEG, MACPAINT, PRODRAW, PCX, ILLUSTRATOREPS, FREEHANDEPS, ARTEXPRESSIONEPS, EPS, PNG
- STATUS/NOSTATUS -- Progress indicator (default: NOSTATUS)
- ASIS -- Original size and position
- AT x y -- Center at position (default: window center)
- USER -- User places manually

Example: placegraphic file "Work:Pictures/Logo.iff" filter iffilbm at 4.0 2.0

## INSERTTEXT
inserttext [FILE filepath] [FILTER name] [progress] [charset]
          [CONVERTQUOTE toggle] [CONVERTDASH toggle]
          [LINEHASLF toggle] [RETAINFORMAT toggle]
          [TEXTCODE code]
          [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Inserts text from a file at the cursor position.
- FILE -- Path to text file
- FILTER -- ASCII, IFFCTXT, IFFFTXT, WORDWORTH
- CONVERTQUOTE -- Convert typographic quotation marks
- CONVERTDASH -- Convert em dashes
- LINEHASLF -- Line break handling
- RETAINFORMAT -- Retain formatting

## EXPORTGRAPHIC
exportgraphic [FILE "file"] [FILTER filtername]
             [STATUS | NOSTATUS] [QUIET | FORCE | ALERT]
             [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec | ID id]

Exports a graphic object.
- FILE -- File name (omit for file selection dialog)
- FILTER -- PICT, TIFF, IFFILBM, GIF, BMP, IFFDR2D, IFFILUS, JPEG, PNG, JPEG2000
- STATUS/NOSTATUS -- Progress indicator
- QUIET/FORCE/ALERT -- Overwrite behavior
- ID -- Object ID (default: current)

Example: exportgraphic file "Ram:Snapshot" filter iffilbm status

## EXPORTTEXT
exporttext [FILE "file"] [FILTER filtername]
          [STATUS | NOSTATUS] [QUIET | FORCE | ALERT]
          [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec]

Exports the selected text.
- FILTER -- ASCII, IFFFTXT, IFFCTXT, WORDWORTH, RTF

## EXPORTPDF
exportpdf [FILE "file"] [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec]

Exports as PDF.

## SETDOCUMENTPATH
setdocumentpath [filepath] [SAVE]

Sets the default document path.
- filepath -- The file path
- SAVE -- Save to settings file

Example: setdocumentpath "PageStream3:Documents"

## SETGRAPHICPATH
setgraphicpath [graphicpath] [SAVE]

Sets the default graphic path.

Example: setgraphicpath "Brilliance:Pictures"

## SETTEXTPATH
settextpath [filepath] [SAVE]

Sets the default text path.

Example: settextpath "Work:Wordworth5/Documents"

## SETSCRATCHPATH
setscratchpath [scratchpath] [SAVE]

Sets the default scratch path.

## SETSCRIPTPATH
setscriptpath [filepath] [SAVE]

Sets the default script path (Amiga only).

Example: setscriptpath "Rexx:"

## SETBACKUP
setbackup [AUTOBACKUP status [COUNT number]]
         [AUTOSAVE status [INTERVAL time]]
         [PATH filepath] [SAVE]

Configures backup and autosave settings.
- AUTOBACKUP -- ON, OFF, TOGGLE
- COUNT -- Number of backup copies
- AUTOSAVE -- ON, OFF, TOGGLE
- INTERVAL -- Autosave interval in minutes
- PATH -- Backup directory
- SAVE -- Save to settings file

Note: TOGGLE must not be used together with SAVE.

Example: setbackup autobackup on autosave on interval 5 save

## SETAUTOCOLUMNS
setautocolumns [ON | OFF | TOGGLE] [LIKE MASTERPAGE | PREVIOUS] [SAVE]

Sets the auto columns mode.

## SELECTONPASTE
selectonpaste [status] [SAVE]

Automatically selects imported/pasted text.
- status -- ON, OFF, TOGGLE
- SAVE -- Save to settings file

## USESCRATCH
usescratch [TRUE | FALSE] [SAVE]

Enables or disables the scratch path.

## FILEFILTER
filefilter [TRUE | FALSE] [SAVE]

Enables or disables file filtering.

## GETDOCUMENTPATH
getdocumentpath

Returns the current document path in RESULT.

## GETGRAPHICPATH
getgraphicpath

Returns the current graphic path in RESULT.

## GETTEXTPATH
gettextpath

Returns the current text path in RESULT.

## GETSCRATCHPATH
getscratchpath

Returns the current scratch path in RESULT.

## GETSCRIPTPATH
getscriptpath

Returns the current script path in RESULT.

## GETAUTOCOLUMNS
getautocolumns [LIKE &flag]

Returns ON or OFF in RESULT. LIKE receives MASTERPAGE or PREVIOUS.

## GETSELECTONPASTE
getselectonpaste

Returns ON or OFF in RESULT.

## GETPASTEINCENTER
getpasteincenter

Returns the paste-in-center status in RESULT.

## GETWINDOWS
getwindows stem [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec]

Returns window count in RESULT. Window names in stem.0, stem.1, etc.

## DRAWBOX
drawbox <left top right bottom> [type]
       [CORNER radius | ECORNER radiusx radiusy]
       [ROTATE angle | SKEW slantangle twistangle | SLANT angle | TWIST angle]
       [ABOUT pointx pointy | ABOUTCENTER]
       [constraint] [printable] [stack]
       [PAGE number | MPG name | DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Draws a new rectangle. Returns object handle in RESULT.
- left top right bottom -- Box coordinates (required)
- type -- NORMAL, ROUND, SCALLOP, BEVEL, INSET
- CORNER -- Corner radius (default: 0)
- ECORNER -- Elliptical corner radius (radiusx radiusy, default: 0)

Example: drawbox 1.75 1.5 2.75 2.5
Example: drawbox 3 3 6 6 inback page "project.doc~8"

## DRAWELLIPSE
drawellipse <centerx centery radiusx radiusy> [type]
           [ANGLES startangle endangle]
           [ROTATE angle | SKEW slantangle twistangle | SLANT angle | TWIST angle]
           [ABOUT pointx pointy | ABOUTCENTER]
           [constraint] [printable] [stack]
           [PAGE number | MPG name | DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Draws a new ellipse. Returns object handle in RESULT.
- centerx centery -- Center coordinates (required)
- radiusx radiusy -- Radius dimensions (required)
- type -- ELLIPSE (default), PIE, ARC
- ANGLES -- Start and end angles (for PIE/ARC)

Example: drawellipse 3 3 1.5 1.5
Example: drawellipse 5.25 6.125 1.5 2.5 pie angles 45 90 print

## DRAWLINE
drawline <left top right bottom>
        [ROTATE angle | SKEW slantangle twistangle | SLANT angle | TWIST angle]
        [ABOUT pointx pointy | ABOUTCENTER]
        [constraint] [printable] [stack]
        [PAGE number | MPG name | DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Draws a new line. Returns object handle in RESULT.
- left top right bottom -- Line endpoint coordinates (required)

Example: drawline 1 1 5 5
Example: drawline 2 1.25 8.5 11 page "project.doc~6" noprint

## DRAWPOLYGON
drawpolygon <centerx centery radiusx radiusy> [type]
           [SIDES number] [OFFSETANGLE angle]
           [DEFLECTION amount] [ANGLEDEFLECTION amount]
           [ROTATE angle | SKEW slantangle twistangle | SLANT angle | TWIST angle]
           [ABOUT pointx pointy | ABOUTCENTER]
           [constraint] [printable] [stack]
           [PAGE number | MPG name | DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Draws a regular polygon. Returns object handle in RESULT.
- centerx centery -- Center point (required)
- radiusx radiusy -- Polygon radius (required)
- type -- NORMAL (default), STAR, PUFFY, SCALLOP, WAVY
- SIDES -- Number of sides (default: 5, must be >2)
- OFFSETANGLE -- Pre-rotation angle (default: 0)
- DEFLECTION -- Spike depth (default: 40%)
- ANGLEDEFLECTION -- Spike angle (default: 0%)

Example: drawpolygon 4.0 5.0 2.0 2.0 STAR SIDES 6

## DRAWSPIRAL
drawspiral x1 y1 ROUNDS n SPACING dist STARTANGLE angle
          [frame] [CONTENTOFFSET x y] [CONTENTSCALE x y]
          [ROTATE angle | SKEW slantangle twistangle | SLANT angle | TWIST angle]
          [ABOUT pointx pointy | ABOUTCENTER]
          [constraint] [printable] [stack]
          [PAGE pagespec | MPG masterpagespec | DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec]

Draws a spiral.
- x1 y1 -- Start coordinates
- ROUNDS -- Number of revolutions
- SPACING -- Spacing between spiral arms
- STARTANGLE -- Start angle

## DRAWGRID
drawgrid <pointx1 pointy1 pointx2 pointy2 |
         POINTS pointx1 pointy1 pointx2 pointy2 pointx3 pointy3 pointx4 pointy4>
        [DIVISIONS horz vert]
        [ROTATE angle | SKEW slantangle twistangle | SLANT angle | TWIST angle]
        [ABOUT pointx pointy | ABOUTCENTER]
        [constraint] [printable] [stack]
        [PAGE number | MPG name | DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Creates a grid object. Returns object handle in RESULT.
- pointx1 pointy1 pointx2 pointy2 -- Rectangular grid (2 corner points)
- POINTS -- Non-rectangular grid (4 corner points, counterclockwise)
- DIVISIONS -- Grid subdivisions horizontal/vertical (default: 4x4)

Example: drawgrid 2 2 6 6 divisions 5 10
Example: drawgrid points 1 1 1 3 5 6 2 3 page "MyDoc~6"

## DRAWTABLE
drawtable <left top right bottom> [ROWS rows] [COLUMNS columns]
         [ROTATE angle | SKEW slantangle twistangle | SLANT angle | TWIST angle]
         [ABOUT pointx pointy | ABOUTCENTER]
         [constraint] [printable] [stack]
         [PAGE pagespec | MPG masterpagespec | DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec]

Creates a table object. Returns object handle in RESULT.
- left top right bottom -- Table coordinates (required)
- ROWS -- Number of rows
- COLUMNS -- Number of columns

## DRAWCOLUMN
drawcolumn <left top right bottom> [COLUMNS number] [GUTTER space]
          [ROTATE angle | SKEW slantangle twistangle | SLANT angle | TWIST angle]
          [ABOUT pointx pointy | ABOUTCENTER]
          [constraint] [printable] [stack]
          [PAGE number | MPG name | DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Draws a new text frame with one or more columns.
- left top right bottom -- Frame coordinates (required)
- COLUMNS -- Number of columns
- GUTTER -- Column spacing

Note: For multi-page or size-dependent columns, use CreateColumns.

Example: drawcolumn 1 1 7.5 10 columns 2 gutter 0.25

## DRAWTEXTOBJ
drawtextobj <left top>
           [ROTATE angle | SKEW slantangle twistangle | SLANT angle | TWIST angle]
           [ABOUT pointx pointy | ABOUTCENTER]
           [constraint] [printable] [stack]
           [PAGE number | MPG name | DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Creates a new text block. Returns object handle in RESULT.
- left top -- Top-left corner of the text block (required)

Example: drawtextobj 1 1
Example: drawtextobj 1 1 rotate 45 inback page "project.doc~8"

## DRAWPICTURE
drawpicture <left top right bottom>
           [CONTENTOFFSET offsetx offsety] [CONTENTSCALE scalex scaley]
           [ROTATE angle | SKEW slantangle twistangle | SLANT angle | TWIST angle]
           [ABOUT pointx pointy | ABOUTCENTER]
           [constraint] [printable] [stack]
           [DPI xdpi ydpi] [frame] [stored]
           [FILE filepath]
           [PAGE number | MPG name | DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]
           [FPO {DEFAULT|FINE|MEDIUM|COARSE|CUSTOM xdpi ydpi}]

Places a picture frame. Returns object handle in RESULT.
- left top right bottom -- Frame coordinates (required)
- CONTENTOFFSET -- Offset within the frame (default: 0,0)
- CONTENTSCALE -- Scale within the frame (default: 100%)
- DPI -- Resolution (xdpi ydpi)
- frame -- FRAMED or FRAMELESS
- stored -- INTERNAL (default) or EXTERNAL
- FILE -- Image file path
- FPO -- Resolution: DEFAULT, FINE, MEDIUM, COARSE, CUSTOM xdpi ydpi

Example: drawpicture 0.5 0.5 2.5 3 dpi 150 150 external

## DRAWEPS
draweps <left top right bottom>
       [CONTENTOFFSET offsetx offsety] [CONTENTSCALE scalex scaley]
       [ROTATE angle | SKEW slantangle twistangle | SLANT angle | TWIST angle]
       [ABOUT pointx pointy | ABOUTCENTER]
       [constraint] [printable] [stack] [frame] [stored]
       [FILE filepath]
       [PAGE number | MPG name | DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Places an EPS frame. Returns object handle in RESULT.
- left top right bottom -- Frame coordinates (required)
- CONTENTOFFSET -- Offset (default: 0,0)
- CONTENTSCALE -- Scale (default: 100%)
- frame -- FRAMED or FRAMELESS
- stored -- INTERNAL (default) or EXTERNAL
- FILE -- EPS file path

Example: draweps 1.75 1.5 2.75 2.5
Example: draweps 3 3 6 6 offset -2 2 contentscale 80 constrain

## CREATEPATH
createpath <left top right bottom>
          [ROTATE angle | SKEW slantangle twistangle | SLANT angle | TWIST angle]
          [ABOUT pointx pointy | ABOUTCENTER]
          [constraint] [printable] [stack]
          [PAGE number | WINDOW name]

Creates a new path. Returns object handle in RESULT.

Example: createpath 1.5 2.5 3.25 6.457

## ADDPOINT
addpoint <MOVETO pointx pointy [join] |
         LINETO pointx pointy [join] |
         CURVETO curvex1 curvey1 curvex2 curvey2 pointx pointy [join] |
         CLOSEPATH>
        [PAGE number | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Adds a point to the current path.
- MOVETO -- First point of a new path/subpath
- LINETO -- Line to the specified point
- CURVETO -- Bezier curve (control point 1, control point 2, endpoint)
- CLOSEPATH -- Closes the open path
- join -- CORNERJOIN (default) or SMOOTHJOIN

Note: The join type only affects interaction with the Reshape tool, not the coordinates.

Example: addpoint moveto 1.0 2.0
Example: addpoint lineto 5.0 2.0
Example: addpoint curveto 5.0 4.0 3.0 6.0 1.0 4.0 smoothjoin
Example: addpoint closepath

## CREATEPOINT
createpoint <NEAR x y> [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Adds a point to an existing path at the nearest location.

Example: createpoint near 5.1 6.25

## EDITPOINT
editpoint [ANCHOR x y] [CONTROLBEFORE x y] [CONTROLAFTER x y]
         [join] [POINTINDEX point]
         [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Edits the coordinates of a path point.
- ANCHOR -- Point coordinates
- CONTROLBEFORE -- Curve handle before the point
- CONTROLAFTER -- Curve handle after the point
- join -- CORNERJOIN or SMOOTHJOIN
- POINTINDEX -- Point number (default: selected). Numbering starts at 0 from the first MOVETO.

## MOVEPOINT
movepoint [OFFSET x y] [POINTINDEX point]
         [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Moves selected path points.

## NUDGEPOINT
nudgepoint <[horz] [vert]> [TAP] [POINTINDEX point]
          [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Moves path points by the configured nudge value.
- horz -- LEFT or RIGHT
- vert -- UP or DOWN
- TAP -- 1/10 of the normal nudge value

## DELETEPOINT
deletepoint [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Deletes the selected path point.

## SPLITPOINT
splitpoint [POINTINDEX point] [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Splits a path at a point. For open paths: two subpaths; for closed paths: an open path.

Example: splitpoint pointindex 23

## CLOSEPATH
closepath [PAGE number | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Closes the selected open path.

## MERGESUBPATHS
mergesubpaths [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec | OBJECTID objectid]

Merges subpaths within a path object.

## SNAPTOGRID
snaptogrid [status] [WINDOW name]

Changes the grid snap status.
- status -- ON, OFF, TOGGLE

Note: Grid snapping only affects the user interface, not script commands.

## EDITPICTURE
editpicture [POSITION left top right bottom [SCALECONTENT]]
           [CONTENTOFFSET offsetx offsety] [CONTENTSCALE scalex scaley]
           [ROTATE angle | SKEW slantangle twistangle | SLANT angle | TWIST angle]
           [ABOUT pointx pointy | ABOUTCENTER]
           [constraint] [printable] [frame] [stored]
           [FILE filepath] [DPI xdpi ydpi]
           [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Sets coordinates and options of a picture frame.

## EDITEPS
editeps [POSITION left top right bottom [SCALECONTENT]]
       [CONTENTOFFSET offsetx offsety] [CONTENTSCALE scalex scaley]
       [ROTATE angle | SKEW slantangle twistangle | SLANT angle | TWIST angle]
       [ABOUT pointx pointy | ABOUTCENTER]
       [constraint] [printable] [frame] [stored]
       [FILE filepath]
       [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Sets coordinates and options of an EPS frame.

Example: editeps position 1.75 1.5 2.75 2.5
Example: editeps offset -2 -2 contentscale 80 constrain

## EDITLINE
editline [POSITION x1 y1 x2 y2 [ADJUST]]
        [ROTATE angle | SKEW slantangle twistangle | SLANT angle | TWIST angle]
        [ABOUT pointx pointy | ABOUTCENTER]
        [constraint] [printable]
        [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec | OBJECTID objectid]

Sets coordinates of a line.

## DISSOLVEEPS
dissolveeps [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Separates an EPS object and its bitmap preview into two separate objects.

## SETEPS
seteps [NAME name] [DESC description]
      [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Sets the name and description of an EPS object.

Example: seteps name "CorporateLogo"

## GETEPS
geteps [POSITION &coord] [NAME &name] [DESC &desc]
      [AUTHOR &author] [COPYRIGHT &copyright]
      [FILEINFO &filestem] [FRAME &flag]
      [CONTENTOFFSET &offset] [CONTENTSCALE &scale]
      [CONTENTROTATION &rotation] [ROTATION &rotation]
      [ABOUT &mode] [CONSTRAIN &flag] [PRINT &flag]
      [DRAWPAGE &n] [DRAWPAGECOUNT &n]
      [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec | OBJECTID objectid]

Queries properties of an EPS object.
- POSITION -- stem: .LEFT, .TOP, .RIGHT, .BOTTOM
- FILEINFO -- stem: .MODE (INTERNAL|EXTERNAL), .FILE, .FORMAT, .DATE, .TIME
- FRAME -- ON or OFF
- CONTENTOFFSET -- stem: .X, .Y
- CONTENTSCALE -- stem: .H, .V
- ROTATION -- stem: .SLANT, .TWIST
- ABOUT -- stem: .MODE (POINT|CENTER), .X, .Y

## CREATECOMPOUND
createcompound [POSITION left top right bottom]
              [ROTATE angle | SKEW slantangle twistangle | SLANT angle | TWIST angle]
              [ABOUT pointx pointy | ABOUTCENTER]
              [constraint] [printable] [stack]
              [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Combines selected shapes into a compound object. Returns object handle in RESULT.

Example: createcompound
Example: createcompound position 1.5 2.5 3.25 6.4 constrain

## CREATEDRAWING
createdrawing [POSITION left top right bottom]
             [CONTENTOFFSET offsetx offsety] [CONTENTSCALE scalex scaley]
             [ROTATE angle | SKEW slantangle twistangle | SLANT angle | TWIST angle]
             [ABOUT pointx pointy | ABOUTCENTER]
             [constraint] [printable] [stack] [frame]
             [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]
             [DRAWING | LAYER] [VISIBLE | INVISIBLE] [EDITABLE | NONEDITABLE]

Creates a new drawing object. Returns object handle in RESULT.
- DRAWING/LAYER -- Drawing type
- VISIBLE/INVISIBLE -- Layer visibility (when LAYER)
- EDITABLE/NONEDITABLE -- Layer editability (when LAYER)

Example: createdrawing
Example: createdrawing position 1.5 2.5 3.25 6.457 contentscale 80.5 constrain

## APPLYATTRIBUTES
applyattributes <AT pointx pointy [stack] | RANGE left top right bottom [stack]>
               [PAGE number | MPG name | DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Applies recorded attributes to a paragraph or object.
- AT -- Apply attributes to paragraph at position
- RANGE -- Apply attributes to all paragraphs in range
- stack -- FRONTMOST (default) or BACKMOST

Example: applyattributes at 1.25 3.3 backmost
Example: applyattributes range 1.25 3.3 1.75 5.25

## INSERTPAGE
insertpage [where] [PAGE number | DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]
          [COUNT number] [INSPREAD [type]]

Inserts page(s).
- where -- BEFORE (default) or AFTER
- COUNT -- Number of pages (default: 1)
- INSPREAD -- DEFAULT, HORIZONTAL, VERTICAL

## DELETEPAGE
deletepage [PAGE number] [TO number] [mode]

Deletes page(s).
- PAGE -- First page to delete (default: current)
- TO -- Last page of a range
- mode -- FORCE, ALERT, QUIET (default)

Example: deletepage page 5 to 7 force

## MOVEPAGE
movepage [PAGE number | DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]
        [TO pagenum] <BEFORE document:...-pagenum | AFTER document:...-pagenum>
        [INSPREAD [DEFAULT | HORIZONTAL | VERTICAL]]

Moves page(s) within a document. Pages cannot be moved outside their chapter or document.

## MAKEPAGESPREAD
makepagespread [PAGE number | DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]
              [TO number] [INSPREAD [HORIZONTAL | VERTICAL]]

Creates a page spread from two or more pages. To dissolve a spread, omit TO.

Example: makepagespread page 1 to 3 vertical
Example: makepagespread page 1

## SETPAGEDESC
setpagedesc text [PAGE number]

Sets the description of a page.

## SETPAGENAME
setpagename newname [PAGE name]

Sets the name of a page.

## SETPAGENUMBERING
setpagenumbering [START] [MASTERPAGE name] [FORMAT type] [LANGUAGE name]
                [PREFIX string] [DOCUMENT name | CHAPTER name | WINDOW name]

Sets page numbering options.
- FORMAT -- DEFAULT, SLONG, ARABIC, ROMANUPPER, ROMANLOWER, ALPHAUPPER, ALPHALOWER
- LANGUAGE -- DEFAULT, AMERICAN, ENGLISH, FRANCAIS, DEUTSCH

## NEWCHAPTER
newchapter chaptername chapter# [PAGESFROMDOCUMENT]
          [DOCUMENT document | CHAPTER document:... | WINDOW document-window]

Creates a new chapter. Returns the new chapter name in RESULT.

Example: newchapter "Part Three" 7

## DELETECHAPTER
deletechapter [CHAPTER name | WINDOW name] [ALERT]

Deletes a chapter.

## MOVECHAPTER
movechapter [CHAPTER name | WINDOW name] <BEFORE newchap# | AFTER newchap# | ATEND>
           [DOCUMENT document | CHAPTER document:... | WINDOW document-window]

Moves a chapter within a document.

## SETCHAPTERDESC
setchapterdesc newdesc [CHAPTER document:... | WINDOW document-window]

Sets the description of a chapter.

## SETCHAPTERNAME
setchaptername name [CHAPTER name | WINDOW name]

Sets the name of a chapter.

## SETCHAPTERNUMBERING
setchapternumbering [START] [MASTERPAGE name] [FORMAT type] [LANGUAGE name]
                   [PREFIX string] [DOCUMENT name | CHAPTER name | WINDOW name]

Sets chapter numbering options.

## NEWMASTERPAGE
newmasterpage masterpagename pagew pageh [PORTRAIT | LANDSCAPE]
            [SINGLE | DOUBLE] [FACING | INDIVIDUAL]
            [DOCUMENT document | CHAPTER document:... | WINDOW document-window]

Creates a new master page.

Example: newmasterpage "Columnar" 8.5 11 landscape double

## DELETEMASTERPAGE
deletemasterpage [MASTERPAGE name]

Deletes a master page.

## MOVEMASTERPAGE
movemasterpage [MASTERPAGE name] [CHAPTER name]

Moves a master page to a different chapter.

## SELECTMASTERPAGE
selectmasterpage [NAME masterpagename] [PAGE number] [stack] [status]
                [RIPPLE | TO number]
                [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW document-window]

Assigns a master page to a page or page range.
- NAME -- Master page name
- stack -- INFRONT or INBACK
- status -- SHOW or HIDE
- RIPPLE -- Apply to all following pages
- TO -- Up to page

Example: selectmasterpage name "Default MPage" page 5 inback
Example: selectmasterpage name "2 Column Layout" ripple

## SETMASTERPAGEDESC
setmasterpagedesc text [MASTERPAGE name]

Sets the description of a master page.

## SETMASTERPAGENAME
setmasterpagename newname [MASTERPAGE oldname]

Renames a master page.

## SETDIMENSIONS
setdimensions pagew pageh [PORTRAIT | LANDSCAPE] [SINGLE | DOUBLE]
             [FACING | INDIVIDUAL] [SAVE]
             [MASTERPAGE document:...-masterpage | DOCUMENT document | WINDOW document-window]

Sets page dimensions.

## SETBLEED
setbleed bleedh bleedv [SAVE]
        [MASTERPAGE document:...-masterpage | DOCUMENT document | WINDOW document-window]

Sets bleed values.

## SETCOLUMNGUIDES
setcolumnguides columns gutter [SAVE] [MASTERPAGE name]

Sets column guides.

Example: setcolumnguides 3 0.25 masterpage "3 Column Layout"

## SETMARGINGUIDES
setmarginguides inside outside top bottom [SAVE] [MASTERPAGE name]

Sets margin guides.
- inside -- Inside/left margin
- outside -- Outside/right margin
- top -- Top margin
- bottom -- Bottom margin

Example: setmarginguides 1 0.75 1 1.25 masterpage "Layout2"

## ADDGUIDES
addguides [type] <AT position> [MPG name]

Adds guide(s).
- type -- HORIZONTAL, VERTICAL, BOTH
- AT -- Position(s) of the guide(s)
- MPG -- Master page name and page

Example: addguides vertical at 2.5 mpg left
Example: addguides horizontal at 2.5 3.5

## DELETEGUIDES
deleteguides [type] <AT position> [MPG name]

Deletes guide(s) at specified positions.

## SETGUIDES
setguides <VERTICAL | HORIZONTAL | BOTH> [MPG name] AT position1 position2 ...

Sets guide positions.

## SETGUIDE
setguide [SNAPALL | SNAPRANGE rangex rangey] [MASTERPAGE name]

Sets guide snap settings.

## SNAPTOGUIDES
snaptoguides [status] [PAGE status] [RULER status] [WINDOW name]

Sets guide snapping.

## SETGRID
setgrid [SNAP gridh gridv] [SNAPOFFSET gridxoffset gridyoffset]
       [SNAPALL | SNAPRANGE rangex rangey]
       [DISPLAYINTERVAL gridh gridv] [DISPLAYOFFSET gridxoffset gridyoffset]
       [SAVE]
       [MASTERPAGE document:...-masterpage | DOCUMENT document | WINDOW document-window]

Sets grid properties.

## DISPLAYGRID
displaygrid <status> [stack] [COLOR red green blue] [WINDOW name]

Controls grid display.
- status -- SHOW, HIDE, TOGGLE (required)
- stack -- INFRONT or INBACK (default: INBACK)
- COLOR -- RGB values, 0-255

Example: displaygrid show infront

## DISPLAYGUIDES
displayguides <status> [stack] [RULER status] [RULERCOLOR r g b]
             [PAGE status] [PAGECOLOR r g b] [WINDOW name]

Controls guide display.

## DISPLAYRULER
displayruler <status> [OFFSET offsetx offsety] [ZERO zerox zeroy]
            [MSYS horzunits vertunits] [DIRECTION horz vert] [WINDOW name]

Controls ruler display.
- status -- SHOW, HIDE, TOGGLE (required)
- OFFSET -- Ruler offset in pixels
- ZERO -- Zero point coordinates
- MSYS -- INCHES, CENTIMETERS, MILLIMETERS, PICAS, POINTS, PRINTERPICAS, PRINTERPOINTS, CICEROS, DIDOTPOINTS, FEET, METERS, SAMEAS
- DIRECTION -- Horizontal: LEFT|RIGHT, Vertical: UP|DOWN

Example: displayruler show offset 30 120 msys inches inches

## LOGREVISION
logrevision [DESCRIPTION text] [VERSION major minor | BUMPREV]
           [USER username] [CHAPTER name | PAGE number | MASTERPAGE name]

Logs a revision entry.

Example: logrevision bumprev
Example: logrevision description "Fixed colors" user "Colleen"

## SETREVISION
setrevision [DESCRIPTION description] [BUMPMINOR | BUMPMAJOR | VERSION major minor]
           [CREATED | MODIFIED] [USER username] [REVISION revh]

Sets revision properties (since v5.0.3.4).

## DELETEREVISION
deleterevision [REVISION revh]

Deletes a revision entry (since v5.0.3.4).

## SETREVISIONTRACKING
setrevisiontracking [ON | OFF | TOGGLE] [SAVE]

Enables or disables revision tracking.

## SETDOCUMENTSTATUS
setdocumentstatus [CHANGED | UNCHANGED] [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW document-window]

Sets the document's changed status.

## REFRESH
refresh [ON | OFF | WAIT | CONTINUE] [ALL | DOCUMENT document | WINDOW document-window]

Toggles screen refresh for faster script execution.
- OFF -- Refresh off, without tracking changes
- WAIT -- Refresh off, tracks what needs to be refreshed
- ON -- Refresh on, discards all tracked refreshes
- CONTINUE -- Refresh on, performs tracked refreshes

Typically used together with LockInterface for better performance.

## CURRENTDOCUMENT
currentdocument [WINDOW name]

Returns the current document name in RESULT.

## CURRENTWINDOW
currentwindow [WINDOW name]

Returns the current window name in RESULT.

## CURRENTPAGE
currentpage [WINDOW name]

Returns the current page number in RESULT.

## CURRENTCHAPTER
currentchapter [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Returns the current chapter name in RESULT.

## CURRENTMASTERPAGE
currentmasterpage [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Returns the current master page name in RESULT.

## CURRENTWINDOWPATH
currentwindowpath

Returns the full window path in RESULT (format: documentname~windowname).

## CURRENTPAGEPATH
currentpagepath

Returns the full page path in RESULT (format: document[:chapter]~pagenum).

## CURRENTCHAPTERPATH
currentchapterpath

Returns the full chapter path in RESULT (format: document[:chapter[:subchapter]]).

## CURRENTMASTERPAGEPATH
currentmasterpagepath

Returns the full master page path in RESULT (format: document[:chapter~]masterpage).

## GETDOCUMENTS
getdocuments stem

Returns document count in RESULT. Names in stem.0, stem.1, etc.

## GETDOCUMENTDESC
getdocumentdesc [DOCUMENT name]

Returns the document description in RESULT.

## GETDOCUMENTAUTHOR
getdocumentauthor [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW document-window]

Returns the document author in RESULT.

## GETDOCUMENTCOPYRIGHT
getdocumentcopyright [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW document-window]

Returns the document copyright in RESULT.

## GETDOCUMENTSTATUS
getdocumentstatus [DOCUMENT name]

Returns "changed" or "unchanged" in RESULT.

## GETCHAPTERS
getchapters stem [DOCUMENT document | CHAPTER document:... | WINDOW document-window]

Returns chapter count in RESULT. Names in stem.0, stem.1, etc.

## GETCHAPTERDESC
getchapterdesc [DOCUMENT name | CHAPTER name]

Returns the chapter description in RESULT.

## GETCHAPTERNUMBER
getchapternumber [DOCUMENT name | CHAPTER name]

Returns the chapter number in RESULT.

## GETCHAPTERNUMBERING
getchapternumbering stem [DOCUMENT name | CHAPTER name | WINDOW name]

Returns chapter numbering info. Results: stem.startmode, stem.start, stem.format, stem.language, stem.prefix.

## GETMASTERPAGES
getmasterpages stem [DOCUMENT document | CHAPTER document:... | WINDOW document-window]

Returns master page count in RESULT. Names in stem.0, stem.1, etc.

## GETMASTERPAGEDESC
getmasterpagedesc [MASTERPAGE name]

Returns the master page description in RESULT.

## GETPAGEDESC
getpagedesc [PAGE number]

Returns the page description in RESULT.

## GETPAGENAME
getpagename [PAGE number]

Returns the page name in RESULT.

## GETPAGENUMBER
getpagenumber [PAGE document:...-pagenum | DOCUMENT document | WINDOW document-window]

Returns the page number in RESULT.

## GETPAGEMASTERPAGE
getpagemasterpage [MASTERPAGE name] [SIDE name] [DEPTH level]
                 [PAGE number | DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Returns the master page assigned to a page.

## GETPAGENUMBERING
getpagenumbering stem [DOCUMENT document | CHAPTER document:... | WINDOW document-window]

Returns page numbering info. Results: stem.startmode, stem.start, stem.lengthmode, stem.length, stem.masterpage, stem.format, stem.language, stem.prefix.

## GETDIMENSIONS
getdimensions stem [MASTERPAGE document:...-masterpage | DOCUMENT document | WINDOW document-window]

Returns page dimensions. Results: stem.width, stem.height, stem.orientation (PORTRAIT|LANDSCAPE), stem.spreads (FACING|INDIVIDUAL), stem.sides (SINGLE|DOUBLE).

## GETDEFAULTPAGESIZES
getdefaultpagesizes namestem [measurement] [custom]
                   [DOCUMENT document | CHAPTER document:... | WINDOW document-window]

Returns default page size list.
- measurement -- STANDARD (default) or USER
- custom -- NOCUSTOM (default) or CUSTOM

Results: Each entry has .name, .width, .height.

## GETBLEED
getbleed stem [MASTERPAGE document:...-masterpage | DOCUMENT document | WINDOW document-window]

Returns bleed values. Results: stem.H, stem.V.

## GETCOLUMNGUIDES
getcolumnguides stem [MASTERPAGE name]

Returns column guide info. Results: stem.count, stem.gutter.

## GETMARGINGUIDES
getmarginguides stem [MASTERPAGE name]

Returns margin guide info. Results: stem.inside, stem.outside, stem.top, stem.bottom.

Example: getmarginguides info

## GETGRID
getgrid stem [MASTERPAGE document:...-masterpage | DOCUMENT document | WINDOW document-window]

Returns grid settings. Results: stem.h, stem.v, stem.x, stem.y, stem.snap (ALL|RANGE), stem.rangeh, stem.rangev, stem.displayh, stem.displayv, stem.displayx, stem.displayy.

## GETGRIDDISPLAY
getgriddisplay [DEPTH layer] [COLOR stem] [WINDOW name]

Returns grid display settings.

## GETGRIDSNAP
getgridsnap [WINDOW name]

Returns grid snap status.

## GETGUIDE
getguide stem [MASTERPAGE name]

Returns guide snap settings. Results: stem.snap, stem.rangeh, stem.rangev.

## GETGUIDES
getguides stem [type] [MPG name]

Returns guide positions. Results in stem.0, stem.1, etc.

## GETGUIDEDISPLAY
getguidedisplay [DEPTH layer] [PAGE flag] [PAGECOLOR stem] [RULER flag] [RULERCOLOR stem] [WINDOW name]

Returns guide display settings.

## GETGUIDESNAP
getguidesnap [WINDOW name]

Returns guide snap status.

## GETRULERDISPLAY
getrulerdisplay [OFFSET stem] [ZERO stem] [MSYS stem] [DIRECTION stem] [WINDOW name]

Returns ruler display settings. OFFSET: .x, .y; ZERO: .x, .y; MSYS: .h, .v; DIRECTION: .h (LEFT|RIGHT), .v (UP|DOWN).

## GETREVISIONS
getrevisions revhlist [DOCUMENT document | CHAPTER document:... | PAGE ... | MASTERPAGE ... | WINDOW ...]

Returns revision handle list (since v5.0.3.4).

## GETREVISION
getrevision [DESCRIPTION &desc] [VERSION &version] [TYPE &type] [USER &username] [REVISION revh]

Returns revision properties (since v5.0.3.4).

## SELECTOBJECT
selectobject <AT pointx pointy [stack] | RANGE left top right bottom [stack] |
             ALL | NONE | INVERT | NEXT | PREVIOUS |
             LINKS | CHAINFIRST | CHAINLAST>
            [PAGE number | MPG name | DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Selects an object.
- AT -- Object at position
- RANGE -- All objects in range
- ALL -- All objects
- NONE -- Deselect
- INVERT -- Invert selection
- NEXT/PREVIOUS -- Next/previous object
- LINKS -- Linked objects
- CHAINFIRST/CHAINLAST -- First/last element of the chain
- stack -- FRONTMOST (default) or BACKMOST

Example: selectobject at 3.5 5.0
Example: selectobject range 1 1 7 10
Example: selectobject all

## SELECTPOINT
selectpoint <AT pointx pointy | ALL | NONE | INVERT | NEXT | PREVIOUS>
           [POINTINDEX point]
           [PAGE number | DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Selects a path point.

## SELECTCELL
selectcell [ROW row] [COLUMN column]
          [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec | OBJECTID objectid]

Selects a table cell.

## SELECTACTIVELAYER
selectactivelayer [layerindex | layername]
                 [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Selects the active layer.

## GETSELECTEDOBJECTS
getselectedobjects stem [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW document-window]

Returns count in RESULT. Object IDs in stem.0, stem.1, etc.

## MOVE
move <OFFSET offsetx offsety | TO x y>
    [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Moves an object by offset or to an absolute position.

## NUDGE
nudge <[horz] [vert]> [TAP]
     [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Nudges an object.
- horz -- LEFT or RIGHT
- vert -- UP or DOWN
- TAP -- 1/10 of the normal nudge value

## ROTATE
rotate angle [ABOUT pointx pointy | ABOUTCENTER]
            [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Rotates an object.

## SCALEOBJECT
scaleobject <SCALE scalex scaley | SIZE newwidth newheight>
           [ABOUT pointx pointy | ABOUTCENTER]
           [CONSTRAIN | FREE]
           [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Scales an object.

## SKEW
skew <SLANT angle | TWIST angle | SKEW slant twist>
    [ABOUT pointx pointy | ABOUTCENTER]
    [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Skews an object.

## TRANSFORM
transform [POSITION left top right bottom]
         [ROTATE angle | SKEW slantangle twistangle | SLANT angle | TWIST angle]
         [ABOUT pointx pointy | ABOUTCENTER]
         [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

General transformation command.

## ALIGN
align [horz] [vert] [scope]
     [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Aligns objects.
- horz -- LEFTALIGN, CENTERALIGN, RIGHTALIGN
- vert -- TOPALIGN, MIDDLEALIGN, BOTTOMALIGN
- scope -- TOPAGE (default), TOMARGINS, TOSELECTION

## DISTRIBUTE
distribute [HORZEVEN | HORZSPACE space | HORZNONE]
          [VERTEVEN | VERTSPACE space | VERTNONE]
          [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Distributes objects evenly.

## DUPLICATE
duplicate [OFFSET offsetx offsety] [COPIES number]
         [ROTATE angle] [SCALE scalex scaley]
         [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Duplicates an object.

## MOVETOPAGE
movetopage [PAGE number | DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Moves an object to a different page.

## BRINGTOFRONT
bringtofront [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Brings an object to the front of the stacking order.

## BRINGFORWARD
bringforward [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Brings an object one step forward in the stacking order.

## SENDTOBACK
sendtoback [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Sends an object to the back of the stacking order.

## SENDBACKWARD
sendbackward [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Sends an object one step backward in the stacking order.

## COPYOBJECT
copyobject [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Copies the selected object to the clipboard.

## CUTOBJECT
cutobject [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Cuts the selected object to the clipboard.

## PASTEOBJECT
pasteobject [PAGE number | MPG name | DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Pastes an object from the clipboard.

## DELETEOBJECT
deleteobject [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Deletes the selected object.

## EDITOBJECT
editobject [POSITION left top right bottom [SCALECONTENT | ADJUST]]
          [ROTATE angle | SKEW slantangle twistangle | SLANT angle | TWIST angle]
          [ABOUT pointx pointy | ABOUTCENTER]
          [constraint] [printable]
          [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Edits object properties.

## LOCK
lock [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Locks an object.

## UNLOCK
unlock [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Unlocks an object.

## CREATEGROUP
creategroup [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Groups selected objects.

## DISSOLVEGROUP
dissolvegroup [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Dissolves a group.

## CREATECOLUMNS
createcolumns [COLUMNS number] [GUTTER space]
             [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Creates columns in a text frame.

## EDITCOMPOUND
editcompound [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Enters a compound object for editing.

## DISSOLVECOMPOUND
dissolvecompound [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Dissolves a compound object.

## DISSOLVEOBJECT
dissolveobject [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Dissolves an object.

## DISSOLVEDRAWING
dissolvedrawing [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Dissolves a drawing object.

## CONVERTTOPATH
converttopath [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Converts an object to a path.

## MERGEPATHS
mergepaths [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Merges selected paths into one.

## SPLITPATHS
splitpaths [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Splits a path into separate paths.

## FLATTENPATH
flattenpath [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Flattens curves in a path to line segments.

## SMOOTHPATH
smoothpath [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Smooths a path.

## SIMPLIFYPATH
simplifypath [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Simplifies a path by removing unnecessary points.

## REVERSEPATH
reversepath [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Reverses the direction of a path.

## ANDPATHS
andpaths [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Boolean intersection of selected paths.

## ORPATHS
orpaths [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Boolean union of selected paths.

## SUBPATHS
subpaths [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Boolean subtraction of selected paths.

## XORPATHS
xorpaths [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Boolean exclusive or of selected paths.

## MAKEMASK
makemask [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Creates a mask from the selected object.

## RELEASEMASK
releasemask [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Releases a mask.

## CLEARMASK
clearmask [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Clears a mask.

## MAKEDRAWINGMASK
makedrawingmask [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Creates a drawing mask.

## RELEASEDRAWINGMASK
releasedrawingmask [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Releases a drawing mask.

## CLEARDRAWINGMASK
cleardrawingmask [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Clears a drawing mask.

## MAKEPICTUREMASK
makepicturemask [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Creates a picture mask.

## RELEASEPICTUREMASK
releasepicturemask [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Releases a picture mask.

## CLEARPICTUREMASK
clearpicturemask [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Clears a picture mask.

## MAKEEPSMASK
makeepsmask [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Creates an EPS mask.

## RELEASEEPSMASK
releaseepsmask [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Releases an EPS mask.

## CLEAREPSMASK
clearepsmask [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Clears an EPS mask.

## GENERATEMASK
generatemask [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Generates a mask automatically.

## GENERATEPICTUREMASK
generatepicturemask [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Generates a picture mask automatically.

## SETTEXTWRAP
settextwrap [WRAP mode] [OFFSET offset]
           [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Sets the text wrap mode for an object.

## GETTEXTWRAP
gettextwrap [WRAP &mode] [OFFSET &offset]
           [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Returns the text wrap mode of an object.

## SETTABLE
settable [ROWS rows] [COLUMNS columns] [CELLGUTTER gutter]
        [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Sets table properties.

## GETTABLE
gettable [ROWS &rows] [COLUMNS &columns] [CELLGUTTER &gutter]
        [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Returns table properties.

## SETCELL
setcell [ROW row] [COLUMN column] [COLSPAN columns] [ROWSPAN rows]
       [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Sets cell properties.

## GETCELL
getcell [ROW row] [COLUMN column] [COLSPAN &columns] [ROWSPAN &rows]
       [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Returns cell properties.

## INSERTCELLCOLUMN
insertcellcolumn [COLUMN column] [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Inserts a table column.

## DELETECELLCOLUMN
deletecellcolumn [COLUMN column] [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Deletes a table column.

## INSERTCELLROW
insertcellrow [ROW row] [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Inserts a table row.

## DELETECELLROW
deletecellrow [ROW row] [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Deletes a table row.

## JOINCELL
joincell [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Joins selected table cells.

## BREAKCELL
breakcell [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Breaks a joined table cell.

## CLEARCELL
clearcell [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Clears the content of a table cell.

## GETOBJECT
getobject [TYPE &type] [POSITION &coord] [NAME &name]
         [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec | OBJECTID objectid]

Returns object type, position (stem: .LEFT, .TOP, .RIGHT, .BOTTOM) and name.

## GETPATH
getpath [POINTS &count] [SUBPATHS &count] [CLOSED &flag]
       [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec | OBJECTID objectid]

Returns path properties.

## GETPATHPOINT
getpathpoint stem [POINTINDEX point]
            [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec | OBJECTID objectid]

Returns path point properties.

## GETPATHPOINTS
getpathpoints stem [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec | OBJECTID objectid]

Returns all path points.

## GETBOX
getbox [TYPE &type] [CORNER &radius] [ECORNER &stem]
      [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec | OBJECTID objectid]

Returns box properties.

## GETELLIPSE
getellipse [TYPE &type] [ANGLES &stem] [CENTER &stem] [RADIUS &stem]
          [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec | OBJECTID objectid]

Returns ellipse properties.

## GETLINE
getline [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec | OBJECTID objectid]

Returns line properties.

## GETPOLYGON
getpolygon [TYPE &type] [SIDES &sides] [OFFSETANGLE &angle]
          [DEFLECTION &amount] [ANGLEDEFLECTION &amount]
          [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec | OBJECTID objectid]

Returns polygon properties.

## GETGRIDOBJECT
getgridobject [ROWS &rows] [COLUMNS &columns]
             [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec | OBJECTID objectid]

Returns grid object properties.

## GETPICTURE
getpicture [POSITION &coord] [FILEINFO &stem] [DPI &stem] [FRAME &flag]
          [CONTENTOFFSET &stem] [CONTENTSCALE &stem] [FPO &stem]
          [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec | OBJECTID objectid]

Returns picture properties.

## GETDRAWING
getdrawing [POSITION &coord] [CONTENTOFFSET &stem] [CONTENTSCALE &stem]
          [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec | OBJECTID objectid]

Returns drawing properties.

## GETGROUP
getgroup [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec | OBJECTID objectid]

Returns group properties.

## GETCOMPOUND
getcompound [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec | OBJECTID objectid]

Returns compound object properties.

## GETCOLUMN
getcolumn [COLUMNS &n] [GUTTER &gutter]
         [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec | OBJECTID objectid]

Returns column properties.

## GETTEXTOBJ
gettextobj [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec | OBJECTID objectid]

Returns text object properties.

## GETTEXTFRAME
gettextframe [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec | OBJECTID objectid]

Returns text frame properties.

## GETROTATION
getrotation [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec | OBJECTID objectid]

Returns the rotation of an object.

## GETOBJECTLOCK
getobjectlock [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW windowspec | OBJECTID objectid]

Returns the lock status of an object.

## EDITTEXT
edittext [AT pointx pointy [stack] | OBJECTID number]
        [PAGE number | DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Places the cursor in a text frame.

## INSERT
insert <text> [CHARACTERSET csetname]
      [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW document~window]

Inserts text at the cursor position.

Example: insert "Hello PageStream!"

## COPYTEXT
copytext [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Copies selected text to the clipboard.

## CUTTEXT
cuttext [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Cuts selected text to the clipboard.

## PASTETEXT
pastetext [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Pastes text from the clipboard.

## DELETETEXT
deletetext [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Deletes the selected text.

## DROPTEXT
droptext [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Drops text.

## SELECTTEXT
selecttext <AT pointx pointy [stack] | WORD | LINE | PARAGRAPH | CHAPTER | ALL | NONE>
          [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Selects text.

## TEXTCURSOR
textcursor <direction> [SELECT]
          [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Positions the text cursor.
- direction -- LEFT, RIGHT, UP, DOWN, WORDLEFT, WORDRIGHT, LINESTART, LINEEND, PARASTART, PARAEND, CHAPTERSTART, CHAPTEREND, ARTICLESTART, ARTICLEEND
- SELECT -- Select text during movement

## FINDTEXT
findtext <text> [CASESENSITIVE] [WHOLEWORD] [WRAPAROUND]
        [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Finds text.

## REPLACETEXT
replacetext <text> <replacement> [CASESENSITIVE] [WHOLEWORD] [WRAPAROUND] [ALL]
           [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Finds and replaces text.

## SETFONT
setfont fontname [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets the font.

Example: setfont "Times"

## SETTYPESIZE
settypesize size [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets the type size.

Example: settypesize 12

## SETTYPEWIDTH
settypewidth width [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets the type width.

## SETTYPEANGLE
settypeangle angle [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets the type angle.

## SETBOLD
setbold [ON | OFF | TOGGLE] [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets bold text style.

## SETITALIC
setitalic [ON | OFF | TOGGLE] [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets italic text style.

## SETUNDERLINE
setunderline [ON | OFF | TOGGLE] [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets underline text style.

## SETOUTLINE
setoutline [ON | OFF | TOGGLE] [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets outline text style.

## SETSHADOW
setshadow [ON | OFF | TOGGLE] [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets shadow text style.

## SETREVERSE
setreverse [ON | OFF | TOGGLE] [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets reverse text style.

## SETNORMAL
setnormal [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Removes all text styles.

## SETSMALLCAPS
setsmallcaps [ON | OFF | TOGGLE] [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets small caps text style.

## SETSUPERSCRIPT
setsuperscript [ON | OFF | TOGGLE] [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets superscript text style.

## SETSUBSCRIPT
setsubscript [ON | OFF | TOGGLE] [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets subscript text style.

## SETSCRIPT
setscript [NONE | SUPERSCRIPT | SUBSCRIPT] [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets script mode (superscript or subscript).

## SETCASE
setcase [NORMAL | UPPER | LOWER | TITLE] [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets text case.

## SETKERNING
setkerning amount [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets kerning amount.

## SETTRACKING
settracking amount [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets tracking amount.

## SETBASELINE
setbaseline amount [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets baseline shift amount.

## GETFONT
getfont [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Returns the current font name in RESULT.

## GETTYPESIZE
gettypesize [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Returns the current type size in RESULT.

## GETTYPEWIDTH
gettypewidth [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Returns the current type width in RESULT.

## GETBASELINE
getbaseline [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Returns the current baseline shift in RESULT.

## SETALIGNMENT
setalignment [LEFT | RIGHT | CENTER | JUSTIFY | FORCELEFT | FORCERIGHT | FORCECENTER | FORCEJUSTIFY]
            [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets paragraph alignment.

## SETLEADING
setleading <FIXED amount | AUTO percent | RELATIVE percent>
          [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets line leading.

## SETBASELINELEADING
setbaselineleading <FIXED amount | AUTO percent | RELATIVE percent>
                  [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets baseline leading.

## SETPARAGRAPHLEADING
setparagraphleading <BEFORE amount> <AFTER amount>
                   [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets paragraph leading (space before/after).

## SETINDENT
setindent left right [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets paragraph indentation.

## SETFIRSTLINE
setfirstline amount [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets first line indent.

## SETHANGING
sethanging amount [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets hanging indent.

## SETTABRULER
settabruler [CLEAR | TAB position [type] [FILL fillchar] [ALIGN alignchar]]
           [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets tab stops.
- CLEAR -- Delete all tab stops
- position -- Tab position
- type -- LEFT, RIGHT, CENTER, DECIMAL
- FILL -- Fill character
- ALIGN -- Alignment character (for DECIMAL)

## SETHYPHENATION
sethyphenation [ON | OFF | TOGGLE] [MINWORD length] [MINBEFORE length]
              [MINAFTER length] [MAXROWS rows]
              [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets hyphenation options.

## SETWIDOWORPHAN
setwidoworphan [WIDOW lines] [ORPHAN lines]
              [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets widow and orphan control.

## SETLASTLINEFLUSH
setlastlineflush [ON | OFF | TOGGLE]
                [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets last line flush justification.

## SETBULLET
setbullet [ON | OFF | TOGGLE] [CHAR character]
         [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets bullet list formatting.

## SETNUMBERED
setnumbered [ON | OFF | TOGGLE] [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets numbered list formatting.

## SETDROPCAP
setdropcap [ON | OFF | TOGGLE] [LINES lines]
          [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets drop cap formatting.

## INSERTBREAK
insertbreak [COLUMN | PAGE | SECTION | FRAME]
           [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Inserts a break (column, page, section, or frame).

## INSERTCHAR
insertchar charcode [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Inserts a character by code.

## INSERTCONTROL
insertcontrol [PAGENUMBER | CHAPTERSTART | SECTIONSTART | ...]
             [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Inserts a control element (page number, chapter start, etc.).

## INSERTDASH
insertdash [EM | EN | DISCRETIONARY | NONBREAKING]
          [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Inserts a dash.

## INSERTDATE
insertdate [FORMAT format] [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Inserts the current date.

## INSERTTIME
inserttime [FORMAT format] [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Inserts the current time.

## INSERTBOOKMARK
insertbookmark name [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Inserts a bookmark.

## DELETEBOOKMARK
deletebookmark name [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Deletes a bookmark.

## EDITBOOKMARK
editbookmark oldname newname [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Renames a bookmark.

## INSERTFIGUREMARK
insertfiguremark [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Inserts a figure mark.

## INSERTINDEXMARK
insertindexmark topic [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Inserts an index mark.

## INSERTINLINEOBJECT
insertinlineobject [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Inserts an inline object.

## INSERTNONBREAKING
insertnonbreaking [SPACE | HYPHEN]
                 [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Inserts a non-breaking space or hyphen.

## BREAKTEXTROUTING
breaktextrouting [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Breaks text routing (chaining) for a text frame.

## SETTEXTROUTING
settextrouting [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number]

Sets text routing (chaining) for a text frame.

## GENERATEINDEX
generateindex [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW document-window]

Generates an index.

## GENERATETOC
generatetoc [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW document-window]

Generates a table of contents.

## GENERATETOF
generatetof [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW document-window]

Generates a table of figures.

## SETCOLOR
setcolor colorname [ALL | FILL | STROKENUMBER n]
        [OBJECT | TEXT | SHADOW | OUTLINE | REVERSE | UNDERLINE |
         RULEABOVE | RULEBELOW | CELLFILL | CELLTOP | CELLBOTTOM |
         CELLLEFT | CELLRIGHT | DROPCAP | BULLET | NUMBERED]
        [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number | STYLETAG name]

Sets the color of an attribute.
- colorname -- Color name
- ALL -- Fill and stroke (default)
- FILL -- Fill only
- STROKENUMBER -- Specific stroke (starting at 0)

Example: setcolor "Red" fill text

## GETCOLORS
getcolors [DOCUMENT document | CHAPTER document:... | WINDOW document-window]

Returns color count and names.

## NEWSTYLETAG
newstyletag name type [NEXTSTYLETAG tagname]
           [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | CHAPTER name]

Creates a new style tag.
- name -- Name of the new style
- type -- CHARACTER, PARAGRAPH, OBJECT, COLOR, FPATTERN, LPATTERN
- NEXTSTYLETAG -- Following style

## DELETESTYLETAG
deletestyletag [REPLACEWITH name] <STYLETAG name>

Deletes a style tag.

Example: deletestyletag replacewith "SubHeadline" styletag "Headline"

## SETSTYLETAG
setstyletag [NEXTSTYLETAG nexttagname] [UNLOCKED | LOCKED]
           [INTERNAL | DRAWING] [NOTOC | TOC]
           [STYLETAG document:...-tagname]

Sets style tag properties.

## SETSTYLETAGNAME
setstyletagname name [STYLETAG name]

Renames a style tag.

Example: setstyletagname "Body Text" styletag "paragraph text"

## BEGINSTYLETAG
beginstyletag [STYLETAG name]

Begins modification of a style tag. Must be paired with EndStyleTag.

## ENDSTYLETAG
endstyletag [STYLETAG name]

Ends modification of a style tag. Must be paired with BeginStyleTag.

## APPENDSTYLETAGS
appendstyletags <FILE filepath | ASK> [type] [progress]
               [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | CHAPTER name]

Loads a style file and appends its styles.
- FILE -- Style file path
- ASK -- File selection dialog
- type -- ALL (default), TEXT, PARAGRAPH, CHARACTER, OBJECT, COLOR
- progress -- STATUS or NOSTATUS

Example: appendstyletags file "Work:Newsletter10" text

## SAVESTYLETAGS
savestyletags [ASK | FILE "file"] [ALL | TEXT | PARAGRAPH | CHARACTER | OBJECT | COLOR]
             [STATUS | NOSTATUS] [QUIET | FORCE | ALERT]
             [DOCUMENT document | CHAPTER document:... | WINDOW document-window]

Saves style tags to a file.

## SETOBJECTSTYLE
setobjectstyle style [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number | STYLETAG name]

Sets the object style.

## SETCHARACTERSTYLE
setcharacterstyle style [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | STYLETAG name]

Sets the character style.

## SETPARAGRAPHSTYLE
setparagraphstyle tagname [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW document-window | STYLETAG document:...-tagname]

Sets the paragraph style.

Example: setparagraphstyle "Body Text"

## SETSTROKESTYLE
setstrokestyle dash [ALL | FILL | STROKENUMBER number] [what]
              [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | OBJECTID number | STYLETAG name]

Sets the stroke style.

## SETFPATTERNSTYLE
setfpatternstyle tagname [ALL | FILL | STROKENUMBER n] [what]
               [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name | ID id | STYLETAG document:...-tagname]

Sets the fill pattern style. Note: STROKENUMBER counts from 0 (unlike the UI, which counts from 1).

## GETSTYLETAGSS
getstyletagss liststem [mode] [DOCUMENT document | CHAPTER document:... | WINDOW document-window]

Returns style tag list.
- mode -- ALL (default), TEXT, PARAGRAPH, CHARACTER, OBJECT, COLOR

## GETSTYLETAG
getstyletag [TYPE &type] [NEXTSTYLETAG &nexttagname]
           [LOCKED &flag] [USAGE &flag] [INTOC &flag]
           [STYLETAG document:...-tagname]

Returns style tag properties.

## GETSTYLETAGDATA
getstyletagdata [TYPEFONT &font] [TYPESIZE &size] [TYPEWIDTH &width]
               [RGBCOLOR &r &g &b] [CMYKCOLOR &c &m &y &k]
               [STYLETAG document:...-tagname]

Returns style tag data.

## GETCHARACTERSTYLE
getcharacterstyle [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW document-window]

Returns the current character style name or MIXED.

## GETPARAGRAPHSTYLE
getparagraphstyle [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW document-window]

Returns the current paragraph style name or MIXED.

## OPENWINDOW
openwindow [DOCUMENT name]

Opens a new window for a document.

## HIDEWINDOW
hidewindow [WINDOW name]

Hides a window.

## REVEALWINDOW
revealwindow [WINDOW name]

Reveals a hidden window.

## SETWINDOWPOS
setwindowpos [AT x y] [SIZE width height] [WINDOW name]

Sets the window position and size.

Example: setwindowpos at 0 -1 size 640 10000

## DISPLAY
display [PAGE <number | shortcut>] [SCALE <custom | preset>]
       [OFFSET offsetx offsety] [WINDOW name]

Changes page, zoom, and offset of a view.
- PAGE -- Page number or: LASTUSED, PREVIOUS, NEXT, UP, DOWN, START, END; or MPG name
- SCALE -- Percentage or: FULLPAGE, FULLPAGEWIDTH, FULLPAGEHEIGHT, FULLPASTEBOARD, FULLPASTEBOARDWIDTH, FULLPASTEBOARDHEIGHT, LASTUSED, ZOOMIN, ZOOMOUT
- OFFSET -- Horizontal and vertical offset

Example: display page 7 scale fullpage
Example: display page previous

## SETTOOLMODE
settoolmode tool [WINDOW name]

Sets the active tool.
- tool -- OBJECT, RESHAPE, CROP, MAGNIFY, TEXT, EYEDROPPER, COLUMN, LINE, BOX, RBOX, ELLIPSE, ARC, PEN, FREEHAND, GRID, ROUTETEXT, LASTUSED, PREVIOUS, NEXT

## MAINTOOLBOX
maintoolbox [OPEN | CLOSE]

Opens or closes the main toolbox.

## SETTOOLBAR
settoolbar [SHOW | HIDE | TOGGLE] [WINDOW name]

Shows or hides the toolbar.

## COLORPALETTE
colorpalette [OPEN | CLOSE]

Opens or closes the color palette.

## LOADSETTINGS
loadsettings [FILE "file" | ASK]

Loads settings from a file.

## SAVESETTINGS
savesettings [FILE "file" | ASK]

Saves settings to a file.

## LOADFONTPREFS
loadfontprefs [FILE "file" | ASK]

Loads font preferences from a file.

## SAVEFONTPREFS
savefontprefs [FILE "file" | ASK]

Saves font preferences to a file.

## LOADPRINTPREFS
loadprintprefs [FILE "file" | ASK]

Loads print preferences from a file.

## SAVEPRINTPREFS
saveprintprefs [FILE "file" | ASK]

Saves print preferences to a file.

## SETMEASUREMENTS
setmeasurements [COORDINATE hmsys vmsys] [RELATIVE rmsys] [TEXT tmsys]
               [FROM <PAGE|SPREAD>] [SAVE]

Sets measurement units.
- Units: INCHES, CENTIMETERS, MILLIMETERS, PICAS, POINTS, PRINTERPOINTS, CICEROS, DIDOTPOINTS, METRICPOINTS, FEET, METERS

## PRINTDOCUMENT
printdocument [SIDES <BOTH|EVEN|ODD>] [SCALE <ACTUAL|FULLPAGE|scale>]
             [COPIES copies] [THUMBNAILS <ON|OFF>]
             [TILING <ON [TILINGOVERLAP amount]|OFF>]
             [PICTURES <ON|OFF>] [DRAWINGS <ON|OFF>]
             [COLLATE <ON|OFF>] [REVERSEORDER <ON|OFF>]
             [PRINTBLANK <ON|OFF>] [PRINTERMARKS <ON|OFF>]
             [MIRROR <ON|OFF>] [NEGATIVE <ON|OFF>]
             [OUTPUT <GRAYSCALE|COLOR|SEPARATIONS|PROCESS|SPOT>]
             [PAGE page | MPG masterpage | PAGERANGE "page,from-to,..."]
             [DOCUMENT document | CHAPTER document:...]

Prints a document.

## UNDO
undo [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Undoes the last action.

## REDO
redo [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Redoes the last undone action.

## QUIT
quit [mode]

Quits PageStream.
- mode -- FORCE (without saving), ALERT (default, ask user), QUIET (quit silently)

## GETVERSION
getversion

Returns the PageStream version string in RESULT.

## GETDISPLAY
getdisplay stem [WINDOW name]

Returns display settings. Results: stem.page, stem.mode, stem.scale, stem.left, stem.top.

## GETSCREENDPI
getscreendpi stem

Returns screen DPI (Amiga only). Results: stem.x, stem.y.

## GETSCREENNAME
getscreenname

Returns the public screen name in RESULT (Amiga only).

## GETPORTNAME
getportname

Returns the ARexx port name in RESULT (Amiga only).

## GETWINDOWPOS
getwindowpos [AT stem] [SIZE stem] [WINDOW name]

Returns window position and size.

Example: getwindowpos at coords size coords

## GETTOOLMODE
gettoolmode [WINDOW document-window]

Returns the current tool mode. Values: OBJECT, RESHAPE, CROP, TEXT, MAGNIFY, EYEDROPPER, COLUMN, LINE, BOX, RBOX, ELLIPSE, ARC, POLYGON, PEN, FREEHAND, GRID, ROUTETEXT, ROTATE, SBOX, BBOX, IBOX, PIE, STAR, SCALLOP, PUFFY, WAVY, LASSO, TABLE.

## GETMEASUREMENTS
getmeasurements [DOCUMENT document | WINDOW document-window]

Returns the current measurement settings.

## GETUNDO
getundo [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Returns the undo status.

## GETREDO
getredo [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Returns the redo status.

## GETERRNUM
geterrnum

Returns the last error number.

## GETERRSTR
geterrstr

Returns the last error text.

## GETCOORDFROMSTRING
getcoordfroms string defaultmeasurementsystem

Converts a measurement string (e.g. "1in") to an internal coordinate value.
- Units: INCHES, CENTIMETERS, MILLIMETERS, PICAS, POINTS, PRINTERPOINTS, CICEROS, DIDOTPOINTS, METRICPOINTS, FEET, METERS

## GETCMDSTRINGFROMCOORD
getcmdstringfromcoord coord measurementtype

Converts an internal coordinate value to a command string (e.g. "1in").

## GETUISTRINGFROMCOORD
getuistringfromcoord coord measurementtype

Converts an internal coordinate value to a UI-formatted string.

## LOCKINTERFACE
lockinterface <TRUE | FALSE>

Locks or unlocks the PageStream interface. WARNING: If the script ends before lockinterface false is called, the interface remains locked and PageStream must be force-quit!

Example: lockinterface true
Example: lockinterface false

## CHECKLOCK
checklock

Checks the current interface lock status.

## RX
rx filepath [DOCUMENT name | WINDOW name]

Executes an external ARexx, Python, or AppleScript script.

Example: rx "PageStream:Scripts/Test"

## EXECUTE
execute filepath

Executes an external script file.

## PLAY
play filepath

Plays a recorded script file.

## STARTRECORDING
startrecording

Starts recording user actions as a script.

## STOPRECORDING
stoprecording

Stops recording user actions.

## BEGINPREFCAPTURE
beginprefcapture [SAVE]

Begins buffering preference changes for faster execution.

## ENDPREFCAPTURE
endprefcapture

Ends buffering and applies preference changes.

## CHARACTERSET
characterset csetname [SAVE]

Sets the character set. Returns the previous one in RESULT.

## BEEP
beep

Flashes the screen (Amiga only).

## ALLOCAREXXREQUESTER
allocarexxrequester name width height

Creates a new dialog box.
- name -- Dialog title
- width -- Inner width in pixels
- height -- Inner height in pixels

Returns dialog handle in RESULT. Must be freed with FreeARexxRequester before script ends.

Example: allocarexxrequester "Test Dialog Box" 400 220

## ALLOCAREXXLIST
allocarexxlist

Creates a list for list controls. Returns list handle in RESULT. Must be freed with FreeARexxList.

## ADDAREXXLIST
addarexxlist handle item

Adds an item to a list. Items are indexed starting at 0.

Example: addarexxlist choices "First choice"

## ADDAREXXGADGET
addarexxgadget dbox type left top width [height]
              [LABEL name] [LABELPOS pos] [STRING text]
              [BORDER style] [CHECKED status]
              [LIST handle] [CURRENT value] [TOTAL value]

Adds a control to a dialog. Returns control handle in RESULT.
- dbox -- Dialog handle
- type -- EXIT, STRING, MULTILINE, TEXT, CHECKBOX, POPUP, CYCLE, SCROLLIST, SLIDER
- left -- Left position
- top -- Top position
- width -- Width
- height -- Height (for MULTILINE and SCROLLIST, minimum: 36)
- LABEL -- Label text
- LABELPOS -- Position: LEFT, RIGHT, ABOVE, ABOVELEFT, ABOVERIGHT, BELOW, BELOWLEFT, BELOWRIGHT, CENTER, CENTERLEFT, CENTERRIGHT, LEFTABOVE, LEFTBELOW, RIGHTABOVE, RIGHTBELOW
- STRING -- Default text
- BORDER -- NONE, RAISED, RECESSED, SHINE, SHADOW, TEXT
- CHECKED -- TRUE or FALSE (for CHECKBOX)
- LIST -- List handle (for POPUP, CYCLE, SCROLLIST)
- CURRENT -- Default list entry or slider position
- TOTAL -- Slider range

## SETAREXXGADGET
setarexxgadget reqhandle objid [HIDDEN <TRUE|FALSE>] [DISABLED <TRUE|FALSE>]
              [CHECKED <TRUE|FALSE>] [HIGHLABEL <TRUE|FALSE>]
              [READONLY <TRUE|FALSE>] [ESCAPE <TRUE|FALSE>]
              [DEFAULT <TRUE|FALSE>] [LABEL string] [STRING string]
              [LEFT num] [TOP num] [WIDTH num] [HEIGHT num]
              [CURRENT num] [TOTAL num] [LABELPOS position]
              [BORDER border_type] [ALIGNMENT <LEFT|CENTER|RIGHT>]
              [ORIENTATION <HORIZONTAL|VERTICAL>] [LIST listhandle]

Changes properties of a dialog control.

## GETAREXXGADGET
getarexxgadget dbhandle ctlhandle attribute

Queries the state of a dialog control.
- attribute -- CHECKED (returns 0/1), STRING (text), CURRENT (selected item)

## DOAREXXREQUESTER
doarexxrequester dbhandle

Displays a dialog and waits for user input. Returns the handle of the pressed EXIT button in RESULT.

## DOREQUESTER
dorequester dbhandle

Displays a dialog and waits for user input (alias for DoARexxRequester). Returns the handle of the pressed EXIT button in RESULT.

## FREEAREXXREQUESTER
freearexxrequester dbhandle

Frees a dialog. Always call to avoid memory leaks.

## FREEAREXXLIST
freearexxlist listhandle

Frees a list. Always call to avoid memory leaks.

## ALERTREQUESTER
alertrequester message [BUTTON1 label] [BUTTON2 label] [BUTTON3 label]

Displays a warning message dialog.

## OPENBUSYREQUESTER
openbusyrequester [MESSAGE message] [ABORT <DISABLED|ENABLED>]
                 [THERMOMETER <DISABLED|ENABLED>]
                 [DELAYEDOPEN <DISABLED|ENABLED>]
                 [TOTAL total] [CURRENT current]

Opens a busy/progress requester. Returns handle in RESULT.

Example: openbusyrequester message "Thinking..." thermometer enabled total 100 current 0

## SETBUSYREQUESTER
setbusyrequester handle [MESSAGE text] [THERMOMETER status]
                       [ABORT status] [TOTAL value] [CURRENT value]

Updates a busy requester.

## GETBUSYREQUESTER
getbusyrequester handle

Checks if the Stop button was pressed. Returns 0 if not pressed, 1 if pressed.

## CLOSEBUSYREQUESTER
closebusyrequester handle

Closes a busy requester.

## GETCHOICE
getchoice MESSAGE message BUTTON1 label [BUTTON2 label] [BUTTON3 label]

Displays a choice dialog (Amiga only).
- MESSAGE -- Message (max. 44 characters)
- BUTTON1 -- Default button (max. 8 characters)
- BUTTON2 -- Cancel button (activatable with Esc)
- BUTTON3 -- Third button

Returns button number in RESULT. Underscore before a letter = keyboard shortcut (e.g. "\_OK").

Example: getchoice message "Click on a button." button1 "\_OK" button2 "\_Cancel"

## GETFILE
getfile [TITLE title] [mode] [PATH name] [FILE name]
       [POSBUTTON label] [NEGBUTTON label]

Displays a file selection dialog.
- mode -- LOAD (default) or SAVE
- RC = 0: Success, file path in RESULT
- RC = 10: Cancelled

Example: getfile TITLE "Save a file" save path "ram:" posbutton "Save"

## GETFILEPATH
getfilepath [PATH path] [TITLE title] [POSBUTTON ok] [NEGBUTTON cancel]

Displays a directory selection dialog.

## GETSTRING
getstring [STRING default] [TITLE label] [POSBUTTON label] [NEGBUTTON label]

Displays a string input dialog (Amiga only). RC = 0 + string in RESULT on success; RC = 10 on cancel.

Example: getstring string "Erase this." title "\_Text" posbutton "\_Yes" negbutton "\_No"

## GETREGION
getregion stem [MESSAGE message]

User drags a region on the page. Results: stem.x1, stem.y1, stem.x2, stem.y2. RC = 0 on success, RC = 10 on cancel.

Example: getregion coord message "Drag to define an area"

## BEGINCOMMANDCAPTURE
begincommandcapture

Begins capturing commands for later playback.

## ENDCOMMANDCAPTURE
endcommandcapture

Ends command capture.
